layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | Buildyboy keeps everything your sessions do, so it can answer questions about the past: what did last month cost,
    | which commands keep failing, how long do I keep Claude waiting, which prompts succeed as jobs? This page covers
    | the
    strong Insights
    | charts, full-text
    strong Search
    | , and
    strong importing
    | history from before you paired a machine.

  h2#insights Insights
  p
    | Open
    strong Insights
    | in the top bar (the page is titled Analytics; on a phone, go to
    code {{ site.url }}/analytics
    | ). Choose
    strong 7 days
    | ,
    strong 30 days
    | (the default) or
    strong 90 days
    | at the top.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="insights-desktop.png" alt="The Insights page: six summary tiles (cost, active time, lines, tokens, cache hit, waiting on you) above a cost chart." caption="Insights: summary tiles first, then charts.")
  h3#tiles The summary tiles
  dl
    dt Cost
    dd Total spend, and how many sessions it came from.
    dt Active time
    dd The sum of session durations, from start to end (or last activity). Idle time inside a session counts.
    dt Lines
    dd Lines added and removed by Claude's edits.
    dt Tokens out
    dd Tokens Claude wrote, with the tokens it read underneath.
    dt Cache hit
    dd
      | How much of the input came from Claude's prompt cache. Higher is cheaper: cached input costs a fraction of
      | fresh input.
    dt Waiting on you
    dd Time sessions spent waiting for a permission answer or idle at the prompt.
  h3#charts The charts
  dl
    dt
      strong Cost
    dd
      | Spend over time, split by
      strong Project
      | ,
      strong Model
      | or
      strong Machine
      | , per
      strong Day
      | ,
      strong Week
      | or
      strong Month
      | . Each session's cost counts on the day it started.
    dt
      strong Tokens
    dd Input, output and cache tokens per day, with the cache hit rate.
    dt
      strong Sessions per day
      | ,
      strong Active time
      | ,
      strong Lines added and removed
    dd Your activity over time.
    dt
      strong Most-used tools
    dd The 12 tools Claude used most, with how many calls failed.
    dt
      strong Most-failed commands
    dd
      | The 10 shell commands that failed most often. A command that fails again and again is usually a missing tool, a
      | wrong path or a test Claude cannot fix, and is worth a look.
    dt
      strong Permission wait
    dd How long sessions waited for you, how many requests were answered, and how fast you answered on average.
    dt
      strong Job success by prompt
    dd For each saved prompt run as a job: its success rate, number of runs, and average cost and duration. Jobs started from a pasted prompt are grouped as Ad-hoc jobs.
    dt
      strong Rate limits
    dd
      | How much of Claude's 5-hour and 7-day usage windows you used over time. Needs the
      a(href="/docs/settings#statusline") statusline bridge
      | .
  +callout(variant="muted")
    @content
      p
        | Days in Insights are UTC days, so near midnight a session can land on the day before or after your local date.

  h2#search Search
  p
    | Press
    strong Search
    | in the top bar (or go to
    code {{ site.url }}/search
    | ) and type. Results appear as you type, up to 50, best match first. Each shows what it is (
    code session
    | ,
    code message
    | ,
    code command
    | or
    code prompt
    | ) and a snippet with your words highlighted. Click a result to jump straight to that moment in the session's
    | timeline; a saved prompt opens in the Composer.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="search-desktop.png" alt="The Search page with a query and a list of matches, each with a kind badge and a highlighted snippet." caption="Search results with highlighted matches.")
  h3#search-what What is searched
  ul
    li everything you and Claude wrote in sessions,
    li every shell command Claude ran,
    li your saved Composer prompts,
    li sessions by their id and folder.
  h3#search-how How to search well
  ul
    li
      | Every word must match, and each word also matches longer words starting with it:
      code rate lim
      | finds "rate limiting".
    li Case and punctuation do not matter.
    li
      | There are no special operators: quotes, OR, NOT and the like are treated as plain words. Add another word to narrow
      | the results instead.
    li Session names are not searched; search for a word from the session's first prompt instead.

  h2#import Importing old history
  p
    | Claude Code keeps a transcript of every session on the machine where it ran, in
    code ~/.claude/projects
    | . The import command sends those transcripts to Buildyboy, so sessions from before you paired the machine, or from
    | places the plugin does not see live (such as some Claude desktop app sessions), show up too.
  p On the machine, from a copy of the Buildyboy code (see Setting up the runner for how to get one):
  pre
    code
      | node cli/bb.ts import                # everything
      | node cli/bb.ts import --since 30     # only transcripts changed in the last 30 days
  p
    | It shows a progress bar and ends with "imported N transcripts (X MB)". Imported sessions appear as ended, with an
    code imported
    | badge, and your redaction rules are applied to them. Running it again does not create duplicate sessions: a
    | session that is already there is matched by its id.
  p
    | The machine must be paired first. To read transcripts from another folder, add
    code --dir
    | followed by the folder.
